I have a small idea: opening and kicking doors with a direction key.
Now, to open a door, you have to press 'o' then a direction.  Couldn't
you make another press of the direction automatically try to open the
door, and if it's locked all presses after that could be kicks?  So
there'd be no need to press 'open' or 'kick'.

It would really be great for nethack on smartphones; saving valuable
buttons.
It would be good for desktop computers too, doors always break my lazy
run of one handed direction presses.

This change wouldn't alter game play at all, and anyone who didn't want
to use it could still use exactly the same method they do now.  You
could make it a option that could be turned on or off.

Only one door would need to be remembered by nethack, not all doors.
1. The player runs into a door and gets 'The door is closed.':  Nethack
remembers this door.
2. The player presses the same direction again:  Character tries to
open the door.
3. The player gets 'The door is locked." (or 'The door resists': repeat
2.)
4. The player presses the same direction again:   Character kicks the
door.
5+. All subsequent presses of the same direction:  Character kicks the
door.
--At any time, if the player presses any other button:  Nethack forgets
about the door.
Next time the player comes to this (closed) door he starts from Number
1 again.

I really can't think of a single possible negative for this change,
only positives.  It would be especially valuable for reducing key
presses and freeing up buttons for other commands when playing on a
phone.

Is there a single player out there who wouldn't like this feature?



